## Assumptions and limitations
Source-provided slope/SE intervals will be approximate normal intervals conditional on the source model and selection, not unbiased post-selection intervals or RNA percentage changes. Bulk-tissue effects cannot identify cell type. Source fine mapping is reused, not recomputed; no colocalization/LD claim. Parent CS67 cultures, GTEx release changes and cross-tissue samples are not independent validation.

Novelty audit: focused EuropePMC PMP22 AND (eQTL OR sQTL) returns57 records. Human enhancer/UTR mechanisms already exist in community primary sources. Candidate rs231016 is a public summary association, not a newly discovered causal mechanism. Broad unquoted 'regulatory variant' query is imprecise (1594 hits, only first100 acquired) and is not an exhaustive negative literature search. A QKI human-Schwann isoform abstract appeared in that broad search; no primary mechanistic conclusion is adopted from it.

